# Framework 16 Goodix fingerprint reader (27c6:609c).
#
# The reader defaults to USB autosuspend (power/control=auto, 2s delay) and it
# cannot signal remote wakeup, so after a system resume the first command the
# goodixmoc driver sends can outlive its 1s timeout. fprintd turns that into a
# VerifyStatus of verify-unknown-error, and hyprlock treats an unknown error as
# fatal: it stops verification without scheduling a retry and the lock screen
# shows "Fingerprint auth disabled (unknown error)" until it is restarted.
#
# Keeping the reader powered removes the resume-time timeout.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="27c6", ATTR{idProduct}=="609c", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
